.TH mnnn-invite 1  "mnnn-invite 2.11.1" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-invite \- Invites: links that connect, bring someone into an org or a review; list, revoke and accept them
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn invite\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invites: links that connect, bring someone into an org or a review; list, revoke and accept them
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
An invite is a signed, expiring link (`muninn://join/…`) that holds no secret. `create` makes one
to connect (default), to join an org (\-\-org) or to review (\-\-review). The other side uses it
with `mnnn invite accept LINK`. `list` shows the links you made and the requests waiting for
you; `revoke` withdraws an unused one.
See `mnnn help users`.
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn invite create \-\-label ben
  mnnn invite create \-\-org research \-\-role viewer
  mnnn invite create \-\-review draft\-1
  mnnn invite list
  mnnn invite revoke 3f2a
  mnnn invite accept muninn://join/…

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-invite\-create(1)
Make an invite link: to connect (default), to an org (\-\-org) or a review (\-\-review)
.TP
mnnn\-invite\-list(1)
The invites you made and the requests waiting for you
.TP
mnnn\-invite\-revoke(1)
Withdraw an invite you made (id or its start)
.TP
mnnn\-invite\-accept(1)
Use an invite link, or accept a request (id or name)
.TP
mnnn\-invite\-decline(1)
Turn down a request
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.11.1
.SH SEE ALSO
